<title>USA: U.N. lists Iraq oil-for-food contracts, companies.</title>
<headline>U.N. lists Iraq oil-for-food contracts, companies.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Here is a list of companies provided by U.N. sources on contracts approved by  overseers for lifting Iraqi crude under terms of the June-December &quot;oil-for-food&quot; deal.</p>
<p>(See also item &quot;Iraq/Ceyhan/Mina al Bakr export schedule - update&quot; which ran at 1314 GMT on Aug 19 for details so far of ships booked to lift Iraqi crude).</p>
<p>    COMPANY		    QUANTITY	  QUALITY	PORT</p>
<p>    Agip/Italy		 2.7 million bbls    Kirkuk	 Ceyhan</p>
<p>    Bayoil/Swiss*	    2.1 million bbls    Kirkuk	 Ceyhan</p>
<p>    Coastal/Aruba**	  2.0 million bbls    Kirkuk	 Ceyhan</p>
<p>    Delta/Turkey	     1.8 million bbls    Kirkuk	 Ceyhan</p>
<p>    Lukoil/Russia	    3.5 million bbls    Kirkuk	 Ceyhan</p>
<p>    Mobil/U.S.		 3.6 million bbls    Kirkuk	 Ceyhan</p>
<p>    OMV/Austria		1.8 million bbls    Kirkuk	 Ceyhan</p>
<p>    Repsol/Spain	     5.4 million bbls    Kirkuk	 Ceyhan</p>
<p>    Rosneft/Russia	   3.5 million bbls    Kirkuk	 Ceyhan</p>
<p>    Samir/Morocco	    4.4 million bbls    Kirkuk	 Ceyhan</p>
<p>    Socap/France	     5.4 million bbls    Kirkuk	 Ceyhan</p>
<p>    Total/France	     6.12 million bbls   Kirkuk	 Ceyhan</p>
<p>    Tupras/Turkey	    13.5 million bbls   Kirkuk	 Ceyhan</p>
<p>    Zarubezhneft/Russia    5.5 million bbls    Kirkuk	 Ceyhan</p>
<p>    SUB-TOTAL		  61.3 million bbls   Kirkuk	 Ceyhan</p>
<p>    Alfa-Eco/Russia	  7.2 million bbls    Basrah	 Mina</p>
<p>    Bayoil/Swiss*	    1.5 million bbls    Basrah	 Mina</p>
<p>    Chevron/U.S.	     3.6 million bbls    Basrah	 Mina</p>
<p>    Coastal/Aruba**	  8.8 million bbls    Basrah	 Mina</p>
<p>    Lukoil/Russia	    2.0 million bbls    Basrah	 Mina</p>
<p>    Nafta Moskva/Russia    2.6 million bbls    Basrah	 Mina</p>
<p>    Rao Mes/Russia	   1.0 million bbls    Basrah	 Mina</p>
<p>    Rosneft/Russia	   2.0 million bbls    Basrah	 Mina</p>
<p>    SUB-TOTAL		  28.7 million bbls   Basrah	 Mina</p>
<p>    TOTAL			90.2 million bbls</p>
<p>* U.S. trader Bayoil's Switzerland-based subsidiary</p>
<p>** U.S. Coastal Corp's refinery is in Aruba, a part of the Dutch Antilles island chain</p>
<p>The above list totals 22 separate contracts through Aug 15, although the U.N. had announced only 18 approvals through that period. The discrepancy can be explained by both Bayoil and Coastal being counted twice on the overseers' list, with each taking both Basrah Light and Kirkuk crudes, but only once on the official U.N. list.</p>
<p>Similarly, Russian companies Lukoil and Rosneft each signed contracts for the two crude types and are listed twice by the U.N. but four times by the overseers.</p>
<p>Tuesday, the U.N. said three more oil contracts were approved by the overseers, bringing the official count to 21 approved out of 25 submitted.</p>
<p>The newest contracts push the total amount of oil contracted to 103.33 million barrels, about 30 million barrels of which so far has been booked to load before the end of the first 90-day period on September 5.</p>
<p>Under the terms of the oil accord, Iraq can export up to $2 billion worth of crude from June 8 to Dec 6, in two equal 90-day instalments.</p>
<p>((--Patrick Connole, NY Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1828))</p>
